    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0560" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg490"/>

                <head>No. 278.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 12, 1883</date>.
                        (Received January 15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 20th ultimo,
                    I have the honor to inclose herewith for your information extract from a report
                    of the committee of privy council for Canada, containing copy of a telegram sent
                    by General MacDougall to Colonel Irvine, the commissioner of the northwest
                    mounted police.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d278-a1.xml" xpointer="d278-a1"/>
            </div>
